		<summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Eric Lengyel: /* Disabling the Console */&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;div&gt;[[File:Console.png|480px|right]]&lt;br /&gt;
The '''Command Console''' window can be opened at any time by pressing the tilde/grave key. (On some non-English keyboards, the key directly below the Escape key should be used.) The window displays a command line and an output buffer as shown in the image to the right. If the C4 Engine was built using the debug settings, the window displays &amp;quot;(Debug)&amp;quot; to the right of the build number.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The console stores a small command history that can be accessed with the up and down arrow keys.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
__TOC__&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;lt;br clear=&amp;quot;right&amp;quot; /&amp;gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
== Core Engine Commands ==&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The following table describes some of the commands that are built into the engine. New commands can be added by an application or plugin module (see below).&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
{| {{Table}}&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablehead|Command|Description}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;address&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Displays the IP address of the local machine. Must be in a network game.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;bind&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''key'' &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;&amp;quot;&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;''command''&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;&amp;quot;&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Binds the key whose name is ''key'' to the command specified by ''command''. Whenever the bound key is pressed in gameplay mode, the specified command is executed.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;body&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Toggles the display of bounding boxes for active rigid bodies.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;cmd&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Displays a list of available console commands.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;disconnect&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Disconnects from a multiplayer game.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;dump&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Writes a list of all currently allocated memory blocks to the file &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;Memory.txt&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;. Leak detection must be turned on.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;exec&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''path''|Executes the file &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;Data/*/''path''.cfg&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;gentex&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Opens the [[Texture Generation]] tool, which renders textures for light projections, environment maps, and impostor textures. (Can only be invoked while a game world is running.)}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;heap&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|(Advanced) Displays memory heap totals in the console.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;load&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''name''|Loads the world &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;''name''.wld&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; for gameplay.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;lrgn&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|(Advanced) Toggles the display of light regions.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;net&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Opens the Network window, which displays various network statistics. (The Network window can also be opened by choosing '''C4 &amp;gt; Network Window'''.)}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;norm&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Toggles the display of normal vectors.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;quit&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Quits the C4 Engine.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;record&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''name''|Starts recording video and/or audio to files that can later be imported as a movie. See [[Recording Movies]] for more information.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;resolve&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''hostname''|Resolves a host name to an IP address. Must be in a network game.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;restore&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''name''|Restore the previously saved game &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;Save/''name''.sav&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;save&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''name''|Save the current game as &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;Save/''name''.sav&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;say&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;&amp;quot;&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;''message''&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;&amp;quot;&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;|Sends a chat message to all players in the current multiplayer game.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablerow|&amp;lt;code&amp;gt;shot&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; ''name''|Takes a [[Screenshots|screenshot]] and saves it as &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;''name''.tga&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; in the user's Documents directory in a subfolder named C4 Engine. If a &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;#&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; character appears in the name, then the name from that point on is replaced with a screenshot count that starts at 1 and gets incremented each time it is used in a screenshot name.}}&lt;br /&gt;
